-pn strips n directory entries from the beginning.

First read the diff and deduce how many directories there are in front 
of the src, include or whatever. Then use -p to strip up until that 
directory.

Let's take an example. The moving clouds diff starts like this:

diff -Nurd --exclude-from=diff_ignore_files.txt 
nethack-3.4.3-orig/dat/endgame.des 
nethack-3.4.3-movingclouds/dat/endgame.des

If you've copied this the diff file to your nethack source root 
directory (that's the one that has the dat, doc, include, src etc. 
directories in it.) Then you need to use -p1 to strip the 
nethack-3.4.3-movingclouds part when you patch with this patch.

Another example is my apllied polearms patch:

diff -bruNX ignore.txt ..\official/src/apply.c ./src/apply.c
--- ..\official/src/apply.c	Mon Dec  8 01:39:14 2003
+++ ./src/apply.c	Mon Aug 22 11:04:08 2005

As it has . as the first directory you can use -p0 or -p1 if you have 
this diff in your nethack source root directory.

Hope this helps.

